/-
Johnson/AtFull/Desc/SpotsWritten.lean: THE FIRST CHAIN's PLACES AT THE FULL SIZE, WRITTEN OUT:
`ProofFile.spotsOf` (Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Places.lean) at the written table of stretches
(`Johnson.AtFull.Cut.cutWritten`, 477 rows) is a written list of 282 places.

Why laws are needed. `spotsOf` calls `headOf` inside two routines that recurse (`byPlace`,
`spotsFrom`), and `headOf` cuts a name with `String.splitOn`, at which the check by Lean's kernel
fails (Johnson/Unfolds/SplitOn.lean). A rewriting of the goal does not reach into a routine's own
text. So: the routines' texts once more over `headK` in `headOf`'s place, the equations between the
two as general laws, and one decision of the kernel at the texts over `headK`.

Definitions.
  `headK`: `headOf`'s text behind `Johnson.Unfolds.splitOn_eq`.
  `byPlaceK`, `spotsFromK`, `spotsOfK`: the texts of `ProofFile.byPlace`, `spotsFrom`, `spotsOf` over it.
  `spotsWritten`: the 282 places: name, place (chain, link, piece, kind), rows. Made from the 477
    rows by a program that follows `spotsFrom`'s text: it only proposes the list: the kernel
    decides the equation.
  `spotDecEq`: equality of places is decidable: an instance in this file alone.
Statements.
  `headOf_eq`, `byPlace_eq`, `spotsFrom_eq`, `spotsOf_eq`: general: at all names and tables.
  `spotsK_written`: BY THE KERNEL: `spotsOfK cutWritten = some spotsWritten`.
  **`spots_written`**: `ProofFile.spotsOf cutWritten = some spotsWritten`.
  Negative test, BY THE KERNEL: `spots_refuse`: with the first row's kind bent to a word that
    `kindName` does not know nothing is returned.
Whose text. `byPlaceK`, `spotsFromK`, `spotsOfK` follow Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Places.lean: this
tree's own file.

Limits. The full size alone. IT SPEAKS OF THE WRITTEN TABLE: that its rows, or the written rounds,
are what the planner makes of any public files is not said here. What a place is worth is
Places.lean's own to say. One negative test at one row. Nothing on soundness. On hiding nothing.

-/
